cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: >-
  Mobilitetsmodellen: machine-learning estimators of intergenerational mobility in Sweden
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2024-01-01"
license: EUPL-1.2
repository-code: https://github.com/olaflaitinen/mobilitetsmodellen
url: https://olaflaitinen.github.io/mobilitetsmodellen
abstract: >-
  Mobilitetsmodellen provides production-grade Python estimators for intergenerational income and
  rank mobility in Sweden. The framework combines classical rank-rank regressions, intergenerational
  income elasticities, and transition-matrix estimators with double machine learning and generalised
  random forests under cross-fitting. Empirical-Bayes shrinkage stabilises municipality-level
  estimates. Comparative modules align Swedish results with OECD IDD conventions.
keywords:
  - intergenerational mobility
  - Sweden
  - rank-rank
  - double machine learning
  - causal forests
  - empirical Bayes
  - EUPL-1.2
  - OSOR
  - FAIR4RS
  - municipality
  - income inequality
